1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
A tour of Island Time 1.22, shown with mock game data.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Island Time is a life sim about Anderson Island, Washington.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,500
There is no bridge: one county ferry connects you to everything.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,000
Each morning starts at your cabin in the woods.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,500
Balance cash, food, health, stress, your job and your home.

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,000
The Ferry tab shows every sailing and plans your trip.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Miss the 7:35 and you are late for work in Lakewood.

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,000
Sailings get cancelled, and the boats after them fill up fast.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,500
Wait it out, walk on, or find another way home.

10
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:45,000
Get around the island by car or on foot.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,500
Your vehicles appear on the map right where you left them.

12
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:54,000
Your phone holds just five apps, so choose carefully.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,500
Island signal is one bar: installs and calls are slow.

14
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:03,000
The Your vehicles card lists every car and your boat.

15
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,500
A weak battery or a flat on one car never touches another.

16
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:12,000
The To-do tab collects your shifts, bills and repairs.

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,500
Each car’s problems show up as their own items.

18
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:21,000
Choose where your skiff lives, and weigh cost, launch and risk.

19
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,500
Tow it with a hitch, or row out to your buoy and cross.

20
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:30,000
Your skiff can carry you to the mainland when the ferry can’t.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,500
Watch the tide, the weather and the gas in the tank.

22
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:39,000
Visitor modes flip the game: the mainland is home.

23
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,500
Weekend regulars can save up, move over and bring the car.

24
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:48,000
The island has no gas station, so you plan every gallon.

25
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,500
Neighbors like Dale help out, for a price.

26
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:57,000
Each game ends with a summary of how your stay went.

27
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,500
Try a harder level, a longer season, or a new home city.

28
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:07,000
Play free in your browser at krazow.github.io/islandtime

